From e56d05d21cee476ef6f5ef10152d4682b34c03a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sully <sully.niu@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:37:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] net: phy: motorcomm: switch back to the in-tree driver

The vendor drop-in replaced the upstream driver wholesale: it lost the DT
bindings (RGMII delays, clock output, auto-sleep), WOL support and the
YT8521/YT8531S fibre handling, and it set .flags = PHY_POLL on every
entry, which is -1 and therefore maps to 0xffffffff in the u32 flags
(PHY_IS_INTERNAL | PHY_RST_AFTER_CLK_EN | PHY_ALWAYS_CALL_SUSPEND).

Restore the in-tree driver. On this board the YT8531 needs its clock
output enabled for the RGMII clock to run - the vendor driver hardcoded
register 0xa012 = 0xd0, the upstream driver expresses the same thing
through the documented binding property:

	phy1_eth2: ethernet-phy@1 {
		motorcomm,clk-out-frequency-hz = <125000000>;
	};

Verified on the ALIENTEK STM32MP257 board (stm32mp257d-stm32mp257dak3-mx):
without that property the MAC DMA reset fails ("Failed to reset the dma" /
"Hw setup failed"), with it the link comes up at 1Gbps and the NFS root
mounts. No driver change is needed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
